    {
      "id": "wuR3LrQ7W-5KgcjuriFNj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -918.6304618572169,
      "y": -50.865665805733414,
      "width": 239.61578369140625,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "AjRcMGncf6rdotStRVjvF",
      "index": "aZl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1638527268,
      "version": 2112,
      "versionNonce": 391064220,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778698047598,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Notice how in this diagram we\nhave increased the size of the\nweb server and the database\nserver. \n\nThat is essentially vertical\nscaling, you will go and throw\nmore capacity to the servers. \n\nThe problem: You will only be\nable to grow your server\nspecifications as much as the\nserver allow it. \n(CPU - Core limits, RAM,\nStorage capacity)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "qmm_c_KSRYcVy8r06tKAS",
      "originalText": "Notice how in this diagram we have increased the size of the web server and the database server. \n\nThat is essentially vertical scaling, you will go and throw more capacity to the servers. \n\nThe problem: You will only be able to grow your server specifications as much as the server allow it. \n(CPU - Core limits, RAM, Storage capacity)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
