      "text": "Horizontal Scaling of Databases - Sharding",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Horizontal Scaling of Databases - Sharding",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1914,
      "versionNonce": 1819365492,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "yjAqemNWUlusdPBdAyG2r",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1911.8531528470385,
      "y": -223.77860431241146,
      "strokeColor": "#000000",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "width": 1387.5787107688338,
      "height": 130,
      "seed": 711873908,
      "groupIds": [],
      "index": "b45Y",
      "frameId": "vkYdCFYZ4tZ4MvCAiFID_",
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "8kfU31YoUsflnC6jbweH8"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1778731080022,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8kfU31YoUsflnC6jbweH8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1916.8531528470385,
      "y": -218.77860431241146,
      "width": 1349.215087890625,
      "height": 120,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "vkYdCFYZ4tZ4MvCAiFID_",
      "index": "b45Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 110203980,
      "version": 296,
      "versionNonce": 1616323060,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778731080022,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We split a large dataset into smaller partitions called shards. Each shard contains a subset of the data and can live on a different server. The system uses a sharding key,\nlike userId or tenantId, to decide where each record belongs. This helps scale storage and write throughput horizontally, but it introduces complexity with cross-shard\nqueries, joins, rebalancing, and distributed transactions.\n\n- Sharding = scalability\n- Replication = availability/resilience",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "yjAqemNWUlusdPBdAyG2r",
      "originalText": "We split a large dataset into smaller partitions called shards. Each shard contains a subset of the data and can live on a different server. The system uses a sharding key, like userId or tenantId, to decide where each record belongs. This helps scale storage and write throughput horizontally, but it introduces complexity with cross-shard queries, joins, rebalancing, and distributed transactions.\n\n- Sharding = scalability\n- Replication = availability/resilience",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
