    },
    {
      "id": "Qj0nu9gYjlNbqZRqTm-Ot",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3642.1356139575446,
      "y": 187.88981196885095,
      "width": 646.75146484375,
      "height": 380,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "4JFBx_EUv2r1gvqqyi_2G",
      "index": "b4bp",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1585470068,
      "version": 944,
      "versionNonce": 221553258,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778907783574,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Raw data is stored in S3, commonly as JSON, CSV, logs, or other source formats.\n\nAWS Glue can run ETL jobs to extract raw data from S3, transform it by cleaning,\nvalidating, deduplicating, enriching, or converting it, and then load the curated\nresult back into S3.\n\nThe curated data is often stored in optimized formats like Parquet and\npartitioned by common query filters such as year, month, day, country, region, or\ntenant.\n\nAWS Glue Data Catalog stores metadata about the data in S3, such as schemas,\ntable definitions, file formats, S3 locations, and partitions.\n\nAthena is a serverless SQL query engine that queries data directly from S3 using\nmetadata from the Glue Data Catalog.\n\nRedshift is a data warehouse for analytics and BI workloads. It can either load\ncurated data from S3 into Redshift tables or query S3 directly using Redshift\nSpectrum.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "KJs2O-3v707VrV9JU9hUm",
      "originalText": "Raw data is stored in S3, commonly as JSON, CSV, logs, or other source formats.\n\nAWS Glue can run ETL jobs to extract raw data from S3, transform it by cleaning, validating, deduplicating, enriching, or converting it, and then load the curated result back into S3.\n\nThe curated data is often stored in optimized formats like Parquet and partitioned by common query filters such as year, month, day, country, region, or tenant.\n\nAWS Glue Data Catalog stores metadata about the data in S3, such as schemas, table definitions, file formats, S3 locations, and partitions.\n\nAthena is a serverless SQL query engine that queries data directly from S3 using metadata from the Glue Data Catalog.\n\nRedshift is a data warehouse for analytics and BI workloads. It can either load curated data from S3 into Redshift tables or query S3 directly using Redshift Spectrum.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
